Subject: [PATCH v1 0/2] arm64: dts: qcom: add OnePlus 7T Pro

Add initial device tree support for the OnePlus 7T Pro (hotdog), tested
on the European HD1913 variant.

The board description covers the memory layout, RPMh regulators, UFS,
USB peripheral mode, GPU, WiFi, volume keys, Samsung S6SY761
touchscreen, ADSP and modem remote processors, and the
bootloader-provided framebuffer.

Native display, audio, Type-C role switching and the remaining
peripherals are intentionally left for separate series as their
dependencies become ready for upstream.

The represented hardware subset has been exercised in the mainline
development tree. This rebased series builds on linux-next 20260810
(3d08ff75a47a), passes dtbs_check without diagnostics and passes
checkpatch --strict apart from the generic MAINTAINERS reminder emitted
for a new DTS. The file is already covered by the Qualcomm ARM64 device
tree entry in MAINTAINERS.

